[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said "one issue, one fix queued". Its own cause table shows two
causes, and the desk's notes name a third. The 412 reports hold three problems, each with a
ticket of its own.

#4471 was closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`),
and the hint won't be fixed because booking-v3 was retired. Neither touches the one-day moves.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 does not close the one-day moves. They are not a date-order bug, so the parser
fix cannot change them. Follow them in their own ticket.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  repo="manuel-martinez-dev/s01e03-what-it-shows"
  issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }}
  status={{ parser: 'fixed', hint: "won't fix", 'one-day': 'open' }}
/>

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so any date with a day of 12 or less comes out flipped: booked 7 April, invite on
4 July. It hits app, email and booking-v2 form reports. Fixed when #4471 closed.

**hint.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says,
and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. Same flipped date, different bug: the fix
is the hint (or the form's reading), not the parser. Only form reports from tenants on
booking-v3. Won't fix: booking-v3 is retired.

**one-day.** No flip at all. A date lands one day early: "Tuesday 6 October showed as
Monday", "every booking in June is one day off", "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday",
"the invite arrived before I made the booking". That points at time zones or the clock
change, not date order. The desk files them under `parser` by tenant, so they are counted
there too. Still open.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, and ten of
the twelve subjects in #4471 are shared across problems ("Month and day swapped?" covers all three). The
subject says what the reporter saw, not what broke. Intake's tag does not help either: it
guesses from the reporter's browser, while the cause depends on the tenant and its form.
Both 0001 and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) were last reviewed in June 2024.

## What to do

- Engineering: the one-day ticket is still open. Look at time zones and the clock change in invite dates.
- Desk: when a report shows a date moved by one day, not swapped, it is not #4471 and it is not fixed.
- Decision 0001 needs a new record: merge on cause (tenant, form, channel), not subject.

